# Restrictions

> Purpose: the one list of global bans. Topic files only list bans unique to them.

## Install & process
- Treat install as copy-only — must **ask + fill** in the same session
- Keep decisions only in chat, or skip writing them to their file (`format.mdc`)
- Start feature work while required Profile fields are `TBD` (unless the dev deferred them)
- Skip intake, or guess brand/stack/features/design/layout — recommend, then get a decision
- Mix phases, skip exit gates, or build a unit that is not in `phase-plan.mdc`
- Start P2 screens before `route-layouts.mdc` is `APPROVED`
- Remove or weaken any default rule; replace the locked UI system (extensions are fine)
- Assume one AI/tool; skip the AI Handoff Log (`multi-ai.mdc`)

## Concept & design
- Invent schema, domain rules, or scope that ignore `concept-domain.mdc`
- Require the dev to supply hex codes/fonts — the AI recommends the design
- Ship harsh or manipulative design (pure black on pure white, big saturated fills, dark patterns)
- Under Layout Responsive: ship one stretched layout, or split into separate mobile/web projects
- Copy a third-party brand, trademarks, copy, or a reference wholesale; leave any source trace in files (`references.mdc`)

## Code & data
- Add `.sql` migrations/seeds; concatenate user input into SQL; edit applied migrations in shared envs
- Hard-delete user records where soft delete (`deleted_at`) is the norm
- Rely on the UI to hide controls instead of enforcing authorization server-side
- Return HTTP `200` with an error-only payload when a proper status exists
- Mix bare native form controls with the custom form system
- Skip shared 404 / status-error / empty screens, skeletons, or lazy load
- Mix Bootstrap/MUI/other themes with the Tailwind product skin
- Turn SEO on without Schema.org JSON-LD

## Secrets & deploy
- Commit secrets, keys, or a filled `.env`; log passwords/tokens/payment data
- Hardcode production hosts, FTP, or DB credentials (web **or** mobile)
- Add a production env key without the same key in `.env.example` **and** GitHub Secrets
- Deploy live with secrets only in a local `.env`
- Run destructive git/db commands without explicit dev confirmation

## Prefer
- Edit existing files over parallel structures; shared tokens and `components/ui/`
- Prepared statements; `.env.example` with keys only
- Order: concept → domain → migrations → API → UI
- Build screens from `route-layouts.mdc`; edit it first when a layout changes
